:null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nHappens in 4.4.1 thru 4.5.dev5.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10300H CPU @ 2.50GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI was working on procedural buildings, using one CSGCombiner3D per room (for lighting reasons), with use_collision=true.  The editor would randomly crash, sometimes running for multiple minutes, sometimes right away, no error messages, nothing reported on the command line.  If I wasn't running the creation code, Godot was happy to continue to run the scene as it was already created.  The script was running in tool mode.\n\nI switched creation code to be in the _physics_process(), just in case the issue was from creating collision shapes in multiple frames that were not sync'd with the physics engine...still crashed.\n\nI changed the creation code to distribute the load...create a single room per frame...still crashed, it just took longer to crash, on average.\n\nI then remembered I had selected Jolt 3D physics engine to speed up the raycasts I was going to be using (not in use yet)...switching the physics engine back to the Godot default resulted in no more crashes.\n\nI created a MRP (below) and found that even a simple test where each CSGCombiner3D only has one box will still crash eventually.  If collisions are off, I can't get it to crash.  If collisions are on it will eventually crash, faster if all objects are added in the same frame (set the \"Per Frame\" value to 0).\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1b73c31-8dd2-4da6-b5cc-34fca04f8540)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen the MRP attached below and just watch the 3D preview window.  You can select how many CSG objects are created in total, and also how many are created per frame.  You can toggle if there are collision shapes or not, and you can select if the CSG additions happen in the _physics_process() or not.  If the collisions are enabled and the Jolt physics engine is selected, the editor eventually crashes on my machine.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[csg-jolt-crash-MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20675481/csg-jolt-crash-MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107366/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}